{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>It shall be righteousness.</b> The meaning: that your fellow will be weighed in the balances of righteousness with you, that he may sleep in his pledge. And according to the translators, there is a difference in places between צדק and צדקה." "And the meaning of <b>the pledge</b> I have already explained in the pericale 'And these are the judgments,' and there I explained it in connection with 'his garment.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The phrase בשמלתו apparently refers to Ibn Ezra's earlier comment on Exodus 22:25, where the same root appears; resolved as 'his garment' following the standard idiom."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:38.407018268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}